use std
into hairdo_png.amni

Imports: os, math, gfx, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes, gfx.scene3d, gfx.hair (used as `hair::`), gfx.hairdo (used as `hairdo::`) and look (the local module look.amni, whose `look_setup(asset)` is used unqualified). This program renders a companion character wearing one of the engine's default hairstyles to a PNG, for checking the styles and for the picker's thumbnails.

`fn num(s const byte[:]) real` returns the value of `parse_flt(s)` (ignore its ok flag).

`fn turn(v float3, a f32) float3` rotates v about the y axis by a radians: `float3 { v.x * cos(a) + v.z * sin(a), v.y, v.z * cos(a) - v.x * sin(a) }`, the sine and cosine computed in real and converted with `linalg::f`.

`fn main()`. Arguments `a` are the os args: a[1] the .glb path, a[2] the output .png path, a[3] the style name, a[4] the shade name, then optional reals with these defaults: a[5] width 512, a[6] height 640, a[7] the camera's turn around the character in degrees 0, a[8] the camera distance in head units 9, a[9] how far below the head's center the camera aims in head units 0.6, a[10] the seed 7. With fewer than five args print "usage: hairdo_png model.glb out.png style shade [w h turn dist drop seed]" and return.
1. `gfx::open_headless(w, h)`; on failure print "gpu: skipped (no device: " plus `gfx::error()` plus ")" and return. `asset = gltf::load(a[1])`; when negative print "load failed: " plus `gltf::error()` and return. Call `look_setup(asset)`.
2. Hide the character's own hair: for every node n of the asset (from `gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first`, count `.nodes.count`) whose `mesh >= 0` and whose mesh name `gltf::text_of(gltf::meshes[gltf::nodes[n].mesh].name)` is "hair", "braid_hair", "tie", "beard" or (only when the environment variable HAIRDO_CAP is unset or empty, read with `env`) "scalp", set `gltf::nodes[n].mesh = -1`.
3. `let sh = hairdo::tone(a[4])`. Tint the scalp cap: for every material m of the asset (`gltf::assets[asset].materials.first` for `.count`) whose `gltf::text_of(gltf::materials[m].name)` is "scalp", set `gltf::materials[m].base_tex = gltf::TexRef { -1, 0 }` and `gltf::materials[m].base = float4 { sh.r * 0.5, sh.g * 0.5, sh.b * 0.5, 1.0 }`.
4. `let item = s3d::add(asset)`; `s3d::place(item, gfx::mat4_identity)`. `let g = hairdo::wear(item, "head", ["skin", "face", "scalp"], a[3], a[4], seed)`. Print "hairdo: " plus a[3] plus " groom " plus g plus " guides " plus (`hair::grooms[g].guides` when g >= 0, else 0) plus " unit " plus `hairdo::unit` plus " center " plus the three components of `hairdo::ctr`. When g < 0 print "hairdo: no head found" and return.
5. Let `u = hairdo::unit`, `mid = hairdo::ctr - float3 { 0.0, drop * u, 0.0 }`, `yaw` = the turn in radians as f32, and `sc = u / 0.1`.
6. Lights: `s3d::sun = s3d::Sun { to_sun: linalg::unit3(float3 { 0.5, 0.6, 0.6 }), rgb: float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }, shadows: false, shadow_far: 10.0, map_size: 2048, .. }`. Five soft rectangle lights, as offsets from mid in the order key, fill, left rim, bounce, right rim: `lit_off = [float3 { 0.1237, 0.5203, 1.1525 }, float3 { -0.8245, 0.1905, 0.9464 }, float3 { -0.5153, 0.4481, -0.7026 }, float3 { 0.0, -0.634, 0.9464 }, float3 { 0.5153, 0.4481, -0.7026 }]`, side axes `lit_ax = [float3 { 0.993, 0.0, -0.119 }, float3 { 0.7, 0.0, 0.7 }, float3 { 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 }, float3 { 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 }, float3 { 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 }]`, sizes `lit_size = [float2 { 0.309, 0.309 }, float2 { 1.03, 1.03 }, float2 { 0.309, 0.721 }, float2 { 1.03, 1.03 }, float2 { 0.309, 0.721 }]` and colors `lit_rgb = [float3 { 3.5, 3.36, 3.15 }, float3 { 0.36, 0.4, 0.44 }, float3 { 3.2, 2.8, 2.32 }, float3 { 0.3, 0.285, 0.27 }, float3 { 3.2, 2.8, 2.32 }]`; for each i call `s3d::add_rect(mid + turn(lit_off[i], yaw), mid + turn(float3 { 0.0, 0.0874, 0.1219 }, yaw), turn(lit_ax[i], yaw), lit_size[i].x, lit_size[i].y, lit_rgb[i], 7.2, i == 0 || i == 2 || i == 4)`.
7. `s3d::sky = s3d::Sky { zenith: float3 { 0.5, 0.5, 0.52 }, horizon: float3 { 0.55, 0.55, 0.57 }, ground: float3 { 0.2, 0.19, 0.18 }, ambient: 1.3, draw: false, backdrop: float3 { 0.0154, 0.0182, 0.0436 }, backdrop_on: true }`.
8. Look: `s3d::look.curve = 2`, `.bloom = 0.03`, `.ssao = true`, `s3d::ao_mode = 1`, `.ao_radius = 0.04`, `.ao_power = 1.2`, `.desaturate = 0.5`, `.saturation = 1.1`, `.contrast = 1.15`, `.sharpen = 0.0`, `.exposure = 1.45`; `s3d::sss_on = true`; `s3d::ssr_on = false`; `s3d::temporal = 1`; `s3d::alpha_to_coverage = true`.
9. Camera: `s3d::view = s3d::Camera { eye: mid + turn(float3 { 0.0, 0.0, dist * u }, yaw), target: mid, up: float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 }, fov_y: 0.3, near: 0.05, far: 30.0 }`. `s3d::init(w, h)`.
10. `let target = gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`. Eight times: if `s3d::render_begin()` then `hair::draw(0.0)` and `s3d::render_end(target)`; then `gfx::flush()`. Save with `gfx::save_png(target, a[2])`, print "hairdo: saved " and that result, then `gfx::close()`.
